WEBVTT

1
00:00:18.031 --> 00:00:21.117
Yes, that's me.

2
00:00:21.137 --> 00:00:23.541
But I'm sure it could be you too.

3
00:00:23.581 --> 00:00:29.933
Have you ever felt that the little devil on your shoulder talks so loudly that it acts for you?

4
00:00:31.293 --> 00:00:33.055
Eat that doughnut!

5
00:00:33.075 --> 00:00:35.196
No, you shouldn't.

6
00:00:35.216 --> 00:00:37.338
Let me tell you a secret.

7
00:00:37.378 --> 00:00:55.712
That little angel and that little devil aren't actually on your shoulders, but in your gut. And your gut holds… drum roll… the gut microbiota: more than 100 trillion bacteria living in symbiosis with you.

8
00:00:56.573 --> 00:01:05.181
In my thesis, I studied how these angel bacteria and devil bacteria influence the reward system.

9
00:01:05.221 --> 00:01:06.422
The what?

10
00:01:06.442 --> 00:01:17.732
The reward system, in the brain, which gives you a feeling of pleasure when it is switched on by drugs, sex, alcohol…

11
00:01:19.146 --> 00:01:23.531
… but also by fatty and/or sugary food.

12
00:01:23.551 --> 00:01:29.999
This system was very useful for our ancestors who, between two mammoths, went through periods of famine.

13
00:01:30.019 --> 00:01:34.143
But today, it mostly leads to a good deal of fat storage.

14
00:01:34.984 --> 00:01:38.665
Worse still, it can lead to obesity.

15
00:01:38.685 --> 00:01:47.168
Worldwide, 13% of the population is obese, and obesity is associated with the deaths of more than 2.8 million people a year.

16
00:01:47.208 --> 00:01:52.269
People with obesity have a completely dysregulated reward system.

17
00:01:52.329 --> 00:02:00.232
Imagine: when they eat that doughnut, they will feel three times less pleasure than a person without obesity.

18
00:02:00.932 --> 00:02:05.517
People with obesity have an overpopulation of devil bacteria.

19
00:02:05.577 --> 00:02:13.406
We think angel bacteria are able to say: “One square of 90% dark chocolate is enough.”

20
00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:18.151
Whereas devil bacteria will say: “Eat the whole bar!”

21
00:02:19.052 --> 00:02:28.342
In my thesis, I am trying to identify these angel bacteria and devil bacteria, and to understand how they influence us.

22
00:02:28.382 --> 00:02:34.208
In practice, I spend my days with little lean mice and little obese mice.

23
00:02:34.228 --> 00:02:38.212
Unfortunately, I can't give them chocolate and ask them: “So, is it good?”

24
00:02:40.912 --> 00:02:46.355
So I have to train them to press a lever to get sugar.

25
00:02:46.395 --> 00:02:51.957
And we have already discovered one angel bacterium: Akkermansia muciniphila.

26
00:02:51.977 --> 00:03:03.983
When we give this angel bacterium to obese mice, their reward system improves: they press the lever as many times as lean mice to get sugar.

27
00:03:04.903 --> 00:03:11.331
I'm super motivated, because I'm convinced we could help defeat this obesity pandemic.

28
00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:16.318
And that, simply thanks to our little angels, we could all be equal when it comes to pleasure.
